      "text": "We begin by generating powers of $2+i$.\n\\begin{align*}\n(2+i)^4 &= \\left( (2+i)^2 \\right)^2 \\\\\n&= \\left( 3+4i \\right)^2 \\\\\n&= 9 + 24i + 16i^2 \\\\\n&= -7 + 24i,\n\\end{align*}\nand\n\\begin{align*}\n(2+i)^3 &= (2+i)(7+24i) \\\\\n&= 14+48i+7i+24i^2 \\\\\n&= -2 + 55i,\n\\end{align*}\nand\n\\begin{align*}\n(2+i)^2 &= 4 + 4i + i^2 \\\\\n&= 3 + 4i.\n\\end{align*}\nThus, the equation becomes\n\\begin{align*}\na(3 + 4i) + b(7 + 24i) + 3 + 4i + b(2i + 1) + a &= 0 \\\\\n&= (a + 10b + a)i + (3 + 7b + 1)b \\\\\n&= (3 + 7b + 1)a + (a + 10b + 3)i = 0.\n\\end{align*}\nFrom this, we know that $3 + 7b + 1$ and $a +10b+3$ must be both 0.  It follows that\n\\[|c| = (3+7b+1) - (a+10b+3) = (a+10b+3) - ((3+7b+1)) = \\boxed{6}.\\]\\(\\blacksquare\\). The answer is 6",
